ink Eurostat main table: Tertiary educational attainment age group 30-34 - Male (Opens new window)">Tertiary educational attainment (male, age group 30-34)</a></td><td class="right" valign="top"><a class="RichTextExtLink ExternalLink" href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/bookmark/9087b697-600e-4a15-8f01-4f692078a245?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="External link Public expenditure on education (% of GDP) (Opens new window)">Public expenditure on education</a></td></tr></tbody></table><table class="wide"><tfoot><tr><td class="Vorspalte" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p><a id="Footnote1c"></a> 1 Full-time equivalents. Classroom teachers, special education teachers and other teachers. Partly differing <a class="RichTextExtLink ExternalLink" href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/cache/metadata/en/educ_uoe_enr_esms.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="External link Eurostat metadata: Pupils and students (Opens new window)">definition</a>.</p>



