xtExtLink ExternalLink" href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/bookmark/65dcfc55-80f4-46af-9451-1e68e86645cb?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="External link Energy imports dependency (Opens new window)">Energy dependency rate</a></td><td class="right" colspan="1" rowspan="1" valign="top"><a class="RichTextExtLink ExternalLink" href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/sdg_07_40__custom_14671188/default/table?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="External link Eurostat main table: Share of renewable energy (Opens new window)">Share of renewable energy</a></td></tr></tbody></table><table class="wide"><tfoot><tr><td class="Vorspalte" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><a id="Footnote1f"></a> 1 The energy dependence shows how an economy is dependent on imports to fulfill its energy needs. It is calculated as net imports divided by the gross available energy. Countries that export more than they import energy have negative values. Gross available energy is a calculated value, defined as: Primary production + Recovered &amp; recycled products + Imports – Exports + Stock changes.</td></tr></tfoot></table>
